    dtps: '1. Adverse drug reaction: Haloperidol (high-potency typical antipsychotic)-induced acute dystonia. 2. Acute psychosis requiring ongoing treatment with a better-tolerated agent.',
    monitoring: 'Observe for return of dystonia in next 24 hours. Monitor for other EPS (parkinsonism, akathisia).',
    counselling: 'Explain that this is a known side effect of Haloperidol, reversible with medication. Emphasize adherence to the new medication. Instruct to report any muscle stiffness, restlessness, or abnormal movements.',
